    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 8,
      "bbox": [
        310,
        168,
        344,
        894
      ],
      "margin_number": 2,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "πεῖσαι What part of the verb? GE pp. 187–188, #195–196. Triremes and the silver to finance them were the basis of Athenian naval power.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 9,
      "bbox": [
        347,
        146,
        383,
        893
      ],
      "margin_number": 6,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "αὐτῷ τῷ ἀργυρίῳ ‘with silver and all’. The Athenian reserves of silver were kept in the treasury on the Acropolis.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 10,
      "bbox": [
        386,
        167,
        421,
        882
      ],
      "margin_number": 9,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "τῆς θεοῦ Don't worry about the apparently masculine ending of θεοῦ. The word θεός can refer either to a god or to a goddess.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 11,
      "bbox": [
        424,
        156,
        442,
        777
      ],
      "margin_number": 16,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ὡς ‘to’, ‘towards’, normally only with persons.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 12,
      "bbox": [
        445,
        156,
        461,
        910
      ],
      "margin_number": 21,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἔγνω The paradigm for this aorist (of γιγνώσκω) is in GE p. 201, #209. Learn it.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 13,
      "bbox": [
        464,
        155,
        501,
        907
      ],
      "margin_number": 22,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ᾠμῶξε Take the augment out of this (so that ω becomes o) and put the iota subscript back above the line (oi-). You should then be able to identify the word.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 14,
      "bbox": [
        504,
        156,
        521,
        744
      ],
      "margin_number": 24,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "γνῶναι The aorist infinitive of γιγνώσκω, GE p. 201, #209.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "vocab_entry",
      "order": 15,
      "bbox": [
        524,
        156,
        558,
        882
      ],
      "margin_number": 27,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "συνοικεῖς This is the normal word for a man and woman living together in marriage.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "order": 16,
      "bbox": [
        579,
        190,
        594,
        372
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Translation for 10B",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 17,
      "bbox": [
        603,
        87,
        638,
        900
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "LAMPITO",
      "text": "So we shall persuade our husbands and force them to make peace. In what way will you be able to persuade your men, who have the triremes and the silver?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 18,
      "bbox": [
        641,
        190,
        655,
        520
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "By money or gifts or by doing what?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 19,
      "bbox": [
        659,
        87,
        712,
        871
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "LYSISTRATA",
      "text": "Oh, but we have prepared this well too, because today we shall take the Acropolis, by seeming to be sacrificing. Having taken it we shall guard it, money and all.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stage_direction",
      "order": 20,
      "bbox": [
        715,
        190,
        730,
        898
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Suddenly Lampito hears a shout and, having heard it, she speaks to Lysistrata.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 21,
      "bbox": [
        734,
        87,
        750,
        649
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "LAM.",
      "text": "Who shouted? Who was responsible for the shout?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 22,
      "bbox": [
        753,
        87,
        829,
        891
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "LYS.",
      "text": "This is what I was talking about. For the old women, who had to take the Acropolis of the goddess, now hold it. But, Lampito, you go off home and put affairs among you [Spartans] in good order, while we go into the Acropolis, which the old women have just taken, and guard it.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "stage_direction",
      "order": 23,
      "bbox": [
        833,
        190,
        888,
        874
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "Lampito, going away, walks along the road which leads to Sparta, while the other women go into the Acropolis and guard it. Suddenly Lysistrata shouts having spotted a man who is approaching.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 24,
      "bbox": [
        892,
        87,
        908,
        569
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "LYS.",
      "text": "Oh, oh, women! Come here to me quickly.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "passage_line",
      "order": 25,
      "bbox": [
        912,
        87,
        927,
        555
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": "KLEONIKE",
      "text": "What is it? Tell me, what is the shout?",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    }
